Additional Use Grant

You may make Production Use of the Licensed Work without purchasing a separate
commercial license only if all of the following are true:

1. The use is by an individual, a non-profit, an educational institution, a
   public-sector entity, or an organization with both:
   a. fewer than 25 employees, and
   b. less than USD 2,000,000 in annual gross revenue.

2. The Licensed Work is used only for one or more of the following:
   a. personal, educational, research, or evaluation purposes,
   b. open-source development,
   c. internal self-hosted workloads of the qualifying organization, or
   d. non-commercial products distributed at no fee.

3. The Licensed Work is not:
   a. provided to third parties as a hosted, managed, or software-as-a-service
      offering,
   b. embedded into a commercial product or appliance distributed to third
      parties,
   c. used by or on behalf of a cloud provider, hyperscaler, platform provider,
      or managed service provider as part of a paid or monetized offering, or
   d. used to develop, operate, market, or provide a Competitive Offering.

For purposes of this license, a Competitive Offering means a product or service
that materially competes with Rango as embedded document database software,
edge synchronization infrastructure, or developer-facing persistence and sync
platform tooling.

If your use does not satisfy every condition above, you must obtain a separate
commercial license from the repository owner before any Production Use.

